-- Migration: drop_public_wallet_wrappers
--
-- PARKED. Do not move this into packages/db/migrations/ until BOTH are true:
--
--   1. Every deployed API image (dev, staging, prod) was built from a commit
--      that contains 20260925013304428_wallet_private_schema, so no running
--      pod calls public.atomic_*. Check each environment's /v1/health SHA
--      against `git merge-base --is-ancestor <that commit> <health sha>`.
--   2. `git grep -n "atomic_\(add\|use\|settle\|reset_expiring\)_credits" -- apps packages`
--      finds no caller outside tests and comments.
--
-- Then: `pnpm migrate:create drop_public_wallet_wrappers`, paste the body below
-- under the generated header, delete this file, and update:
--   - tests/migration/credit-rpc-overloads.test.ts (the public.* assertions,
--     including the atomic_use_credits wrapper rows),
--   - packages/db/scripts/atomic-use-credits-balance-guard.integration.test.ts
--     (call kortix_wallet.debit_credits directly),
--   - tests/src/flows/security-backlog.flow.ts SEC-K (a dropped name answers
--     404 PGRST202, which the flow already accepts).
--
-- The wallet (apps/api/src/billing/wallet) calls kortix_wallet.* directly and
-- does not depend on these wrappers.

-- mixed-version-safe: every deployed API image calls kortix_wallet.* (precondition 1); the wrappers have no other caller (precondition 2).

DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.atomic_add_credits(uuid, numeric, boolean, text, timestamp with time zone, text, text, text);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.atomic_use_credits(uuid, numeric, text, text, text);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.atomic_settle_credits(uuid, numeric, text, text, text);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.atomic_reset_expiring_credits(uuid, numeric, text, text);
